# Alembic Database Migrations

This directory contains database migration scripts for the Resume Generator MCP Server.

## Commands

### Create a new migration
```bash
alembic revision --autogenerate -m "Description of changes"
```

### Apply migrations (upgrade to latest)
```bash
alembic upgrade head
```

### Rollback one migration
```bash
alembic downgrade -1
```

### View migration history
```bash
alembic history
```

### View current revision
```bash
alembic current
```

## Initial Setup

The database tables are automatically created on application startup using SQLAlchemy's `create_all()`.
However, for future schema changes, use Alembic migrations to track and apply changes systematically.

## Note

Make sure to have your `.env` file configured with the `DATABASE_URL` before running migrations.
